# 16. Wazuh File Integrity Monitoring

One of the important Wazuh capabilities is **File Integrity Monitoring (FIM)**.

You learned the basics on Day 18.

Example:

```text
/etc/important.conf
        ↓
File modified
        ↓
Wazuh detects change
        ↓
Alert
        ↓
SOC investigates
```

The analyst can investigate:

```text
What changed?
When did it change?
Who changed it?
Was the change authorized?
Was there related process activity?
Was there network activity?
```

