# 18. Day 23 Practical Challenge 🕵️

Imagine your Wazuh dashboard reports:

```text
ALERT:
Multiple SSH Authentication Failures

Host:
Linux-Server-01

Source IP:
192.168.1.50

Username:
admin
```

You discover:

```text
10:01 — Failed SSH login
10:01 — Failed SSH login
10:01 — Failed SSH login
10:02 — Successful SSH login
10:04 — sudo command
10:06 — New process
10:07 — Network connection
```

### Task 1 — Identify the initial alert

```text
Multiple SSH authentication failures
```

### Task 2 — Identify the source

```text
192.168.1.50
```

### Task 3 — Identify the account

```text
admin
```

### Task 4 — Find related activity

```text
Successful login
        ↓
sudo
        ↓
Process
        ↓
Network
```

### Task 5 — Determine whether more investigation is required

```text
Yes
```

### Task 6 — Write the analyst finding

Example:

```text
Multiple SSH authentication failures from 192.168.1.50
were followed by a successful login to the admin account.
Subsequent privileged, process, and network activity was
observed. Further investigation is required to determine
whether the activity was authorized.
```

